remembering fallen trooper micah may  while saving a life nevada highway  patrol is teamed up with by talent to  host a blood drive in honor of the  fallen trooper this morning bianca  holman shares how you can participate  and joins us live this morning from nhp  headquarters bianca good morning  hey good morning john so we are near  sunset and decatur the headquarters of  nhp and this is where the blood drive  will be right here  starting at 10 a.m and ending at 5 p.m  and it again is all in honor of trooper  micah may trooper micah may was laid to  rest on friday he was hit while trying  to stop a carjacking suspect and he  didn't make it passing away at umc  hospital a father husband brother and  son those close to him say he dedicated  his life to selfless service so in honor  of may's courage and integrity nevada  highway patrol is holding a blood drive  to help save lives brittany estrella  vitalent says people who are in  chemotherapy and those who need blood  transfusion from car crashes childbirth  or sickle cell are in dire need of  donations  o negative is a type of blood that is  the universal blood type and there is an  urgent need for this type specifically  because this is the blood type that is  utilized in a trauma center situation  when there are seconds remaining to save  the life of a hospital patient  and this  type is specifically needed at this time  but with the pandemic we continue to see  hundreds of blood drives that are  canceled every month due to the pandemic  there are still many business closures  that are taking place right now and a  lot of businesses that are operating  remotely so we encourage anyone who is  feeling healthy and feeling well to come  donate blood  so here are the details listed on your  screen the blood drive at nhp training  room from 10 a.m to 5 p.m takes about an  hour of your time from check-in to  donation and then the observation period  so you can register in advance but again  they will have some spots open for  walk-ins but again they encourage you to  plan in advance and register online also  be sure to bring a mask all those  donating and of course employees and  workers here at nhp will be wearing  their mass following guidelines  reporting live from sunset in decatur  bianca holman 8 news now bianca thank  you very much
 

